WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:04.699
You chose the edge for an
application and locked its origin,

3
00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:06.650
so a direct request is refused.

4
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.588
You checked TLS, and tested failover.

5
00:00:09.588 --> 00:00:13.664
You checked that the pilot subnet's
egress routes to Azure Firewall,

6
00:00:13.664 --> 00:00:17.521
with threat intelligence and
intrusion detection in deny mode,

7
00:00:17.521 --> 00:00:19.850
and found the denied request in its log.

8
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:24.784
The evidence an I S S O keeps from this
module: the profile, origin group,

9
00:00:24.784 --> 00:00:28.593
route and access-restriction
exports; the TLS policy;

10
00:00:28.593 --> 00:00:32.142
the refused direct request
and the failover test;

11
00:00:32.142 --> 00:00:35.344
the firewall policy
export and route tables;

12
00:00:35.344 --> 00:00:40.538
the denied request and its log row;
and the bypass and allow-list register.

13
00:00:40.538 --> 00:00:44.031
Next is Module 4: Private
Link, D N S and Key Vault,

14
00:00:44.031 --> 00:00:49.700
taking pass off the internet and
putting vaults behind role-based access.
